{
  "requirement": "The review prompt MUST direct the reviewer not to re-raise the decisions and open choices that the brief lists.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement text is: \"The review prompt MUST direct the reviewer not to re-raise the decisions and open choices that the brief lists.\" It has no structural obligation. It names no library, algorithm, signature, type, field or delegation interface. It only requires the review prompt to contain an instruction.\n\nI considered one candidate, the clause \"MUST direct the reviewer not to re-raise…\". Any wording or placement of that instruction, anywhere in the prompt, gives the same reviewer behavior and meets the clause. So how the prompt is built is discretionary, and the obligation is about content and behavior only.\n\nThe supplied root is `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/references/review-prompt.md`. Its first paragraph, under `section[Requirement group review]`, says the agent that started the reviewer provides \"a brief: what the user asked for, the decisions already made, and the open choices already noted. Don't re-raise those.\" That is the instruction the requirement asks for, and it covers both the decisions and the open choices.\n\nNo further implementation root is needed. No acknowledgments were supplied, and none are needed.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one obligation. The review prompt MUST direct the reviewer not to re-raise the decisions and open choices that the brief lists. The prompt is static text, so the test checks the shipped prompt file directly.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_review_prompt_does_not_reraise_the_brief]` loads the prompt with `review_prompt()`, which reads `references/review-prompt.md` from the `habeas-requirements` skill. It collapses line wrapping with `collapse` and calls `assert_text_in_order`, which panics if a phrase is missing or out of order. It asserts two phrases in order:\n- \"the decisions already made, and the open choices already noted\". This ties the instruction to what the brief lists.\n- \"Don't re-raise those\". This is the instruction not to re-raise.\n\nThe shipped text in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/references/review-prompt.md` reads \"...the decisions already made, and the open choices already noted. Don't re-raise those.\" The assertions match it. A prompt that dropped the directive, or stopped pointing it at the brief's decisions and open choices, would fail the test.\n\nThis covers the whole obligation. The requirement names no other modes or boundary cases, and I found no gaps.",
